tion: (1) Backend generates unique CSRF token per session in Set-Cookie header, (2) Frontend reads from DOM, (3) Frontend sends in X-CSRF-Token header on POST/PUT/DELETE. Ensure SameSite=Lax or Strict on all cookies.\",\n      \"impact\": \"Prevents cross-origin form attacks\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"priority\": \"critical\",\n      \"category\": \"security-headers\",\n      \"action\": \"Add Content-Security-Policy header with script-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'. Add X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, X-Frame-Options: DENY\",\n      \"impact\": \"Prevents inline script injection; blocks framing attacks; forces MIME type validation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"category\": \"error-handling\",\n      \"action\": \"Sanitize backend error messages before display: (1) Log full error server-side only, (2) Return generic user-facing message, (3) Never include infrastructure details, (4) Use DOMPurify if HTML rendering needed\",\n      \"impact\": \"Prevents information disclosure; blocks XSS via error injection\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"category\": \"authentication\",\n      \"action\": \"On 401 response: (1) Clear token, (2) Redirect to /login, (3) Show notification 'Session expired, please log in again', (4) Preserve intended destination for post-login redirect\",\n      \"impact\": \"Prevents inconsistent UI state; improves UX\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"category\": \"data-protection\",\n      \"action\": \"Encrypt sensitive data before localStorage caching. Use TweetNaCl.js or libsodium.js for symmetric encryption with user-specific key. Or: migrate to sessionStorage for session-only data.\",\n      \"impact\": \"Protects cached sensitive data from XSS; data cleared on browser close\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"priority\": \"medium\",\n      \"category\": \"input-validation\",\n      \"action\": \"Implement domain whitelist for URL validation: maintain list of trusted API domains; reject any URL not in whitelist. Check both protocol AND domain.\",\n      \"impact\": \"Prevents open redirect attacks to attacker domains\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"priority\": \"medium\",\n      \"category\": \"deserialization\",\n      \"action\": \"Add schema validation to parseConfig(): use a library like Zod or Joi to validate config shape and field types before use\",\n      \"impact\": \"Prevents prototype pollution and unexpected object structures\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"priority\": \"medium\",\n      \"category\": \"environment\",\n      \"action\": \"Require explicit VITE_API_BASE in .env for all environments. Provide build-time validation that it matches expected domain pattern. Never fallback to localhost in production builds.\",\n      \"impact\": \"Prevents configuration errors leaking internal URLs\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"priority\": \"low\",\n      \"category\": \"xss\",\n      \"action\": \"Never use dangerouslySetInnerHTML on transcript/event data. Keep React's default string escaping. If HTML rendering needed, use DOMPurify.sanitize().\",\n      \"impact\": \"Prevents XSS via transcript injection\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"total_vulnerabilities\": 11,\n    \"critical\": 3,\n    \"high\": 5,\n    \"medium\": 2,\n    \"low\": 1,\n    \"primary_risks\": [\n      \"Token stored in localStorage (XSS-accessible)\",\n      \"No CSRF protection on state-changing requests\",\n      \"Error messages leak infrastructure details and could enable XSS\",\n      \"Sensitive data cached unencrypted in localStorage\",\n      \"Missing security headers (CSP, X-Frame-Options)\"\n    ],\n    \"assessment\": \"The frontend has significant authentication and data protection gaps. The localStorage-based token storage is the most critical issue—XSS on any third-party script can steal the JWT. CSRF protection is missing, and error handling exposes internal infrastructure. Immediate action needed on the top 3 critical recommendations.\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Key findings:**\n\n1. **Token theft vulnerability (HIGH)**: JWT in `localStorage` is readable by any JavaScript, including XSS payloads. Switch to httpOnly cookies immediately.\n\n2. **Error message XSS (HIGH)**: Line 35 in `src/api.ts` passes unsanitized backend responses directly to the error thrown. A malicious backend could inject scripts.\n\n3. **Information disclosure (HIGH)**: Error messages reveal Mongo, LiveKit, and internal URLs, aiding reconnaissance.\n\n4. **Missing CSRF tokens (HIGH)**: No cross-site request forgery protection on POST/PUT/DELETE operations.\n\n5. **Plaintext sensitive cache (MEDIUM)**: `src/utils/cache.ts` stores data unencrypted in localStorage.\n\nAll recommendations are ordered by priority—start with httpOnly cookies, CSRF tokens, and CSP headers.\n",
